msgid "Documentation for the latest version of Qiskit bosons"
msgstr "Dokumentasyon para sa pinakabagong bersyon ng Qiskit bosons"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit Bosons"
msgstr "Qiskit Bosons"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit Bosons {#qiskit-bosons}"
msgstr "Qiskit Bosons {#qiskit-bosons}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit-bosons` extends the Qiskit SDK with tools for working on bosonic systems. Within its scope it provides the following:\n"
msgstr "Pinalalawak ng `qiskit-bosons` ang Qiskit SDK gamit ang mga tool para sa paggawa sa mga bosonic system. Sa saklaw nito, nagbibigay ito ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An efficient data structure for the representation and manipulation of bosonic operators\n"
msgstr "Isang mahusay na data structure para sa representasyon at manipulasyon ng mga bosonic operator\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A framework for implementing boson-to-qubit encodings, built around shared level encodings (unary with or without projectors, standard binary, Gray), and a library of common mappers\n"
msgstr "Isang framework para sa pagpapatupad ng mga boson-to-qubit encoding, na nakabatay sa mga shared level encoding (unary na may o walang projector, standard binary, Gray), at isang library ng mga karaniwang mapper\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A framework and library of gates for expressing bosonic circuits\n"
msgstr "Isang framework at library ng mga gate para sa pagpapahayag ng mga bosonic circuit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A transpilation pipeline integrated with the Qiskit transpiler process to synthesize bosonic circuits into qubit-based circuits\n"
msgstr "Isang transpilation pipeline na isinama sa Qiskit transpiler process para i-synthesize ang mga bosonic circuit tungo sa mga circuit na nakabatay sa qubit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get started {#get-started}"
msgstr "Magsimula {#get-started}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This package covers the whole path from a bosonic operator to a qubit circuit. You can work in the bosonic regime with both, operator and circuit representation, before you choose a truncation and a boson-to-qubit encoding that plug into the multi-representation transpiler pipeline of Qiskit.\n"
msgstr "Sinasaklaw ng package na ito ang buong landas mula sa isang bosonic operator hanggang sa isang qubit circuit. Maaari kang gumawa sa bosonic regime gamit ang parehong representasyon ng operator at ng circuit, bago ka pumili ng truncation at ng boson-to-qubit encoding na isasaksak sa multi-representation transpiler pipeline ng Qiskit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All of these features are explained in [several guides](/addons/qiskit-bosons/guides/overview) to help you get started. For an end-to-end overview, start with the [Bose-Hubbard guide](/addons/qiskit-bosons/guides/bose-hubbard).\n"
msgstr "Ipinapaliwanag ang lahat ng feature na ito sa [ilang gabay](/addons/qiskit-bosons/guides/overview) para matulungan kang magsimula. Para sa end-to-end na pangkalahatang-ideya, magsimula sa [gabay sa Bose-Hubbard](/addons/qiskit-bosons/guides/bose-hubbard).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Technical discussion {#technical-discussion}"
msgstr "Teknikal na talakayan {#technical-discussion}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Design intentions {#design-intentions}"
msgstr "Mga layunin sa disenyo {#design-intentions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This package is deliberately designed to align with Qiskit: it builds on a core implemented in Rust and provides first-party language bindings to Python. Its API intends to draw parallels to Qiskit in order to seamlessly integrate into the workflows of users with experience in programming Qiskit. While there exists no C API right now, the architecture is set up to support one if the need for one ever arises in the future. The architecture of this package is also deliberately analogous to that of [qiskit-fermions](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-fermions).\n"
msgstr "Sadyang idinisenyo ang package na ito para umayon sa Qiskit: nakabatay ito sa core na ipinatupad sa Rust at nagbibigay ng first-party na language binding sa Python. Layunin ng API nito na gumawa ng mga pagkakahalintulad sa Qiskit para maayos na maisama sa mga workflow ng mga user na may karanasan sa pag-program ng Qiskit. Bagaman wala pang C API sa ngayon, nakahanda ang arkitektura para suportahan ang isa kung sakaling kailanganin ito sa hinaharap. Sadya ring kahalintulad ang arkitektura ng package na ito sa [qiskit-fermions](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-fermions).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A core principle to the design of `qiskit-bosons` was the decoupling of its bosonic circuit representation from its qubitized form. To be more precise: the bosonic circuits are meaningful by themselves and do not require a mapping to qubit space to be interpretable. Furthermore, the bosonic circuit representation cannot make any assumptions about the truncation and boson-to-qubit encoding applied later on. Both enter only at transpile time.\n"
msgstr "Isang pangunahing prinsipyo sa disenyo ng `qiskit-bosons` ang paghihiwalay ng bosonic circuit representation nito mula sa qubitized na anyo nito. Para maging mas tiyak: may sariling kabuluhan ang mga bosonic circuit at hindi nangangailangan ng mapping sa qubit space para maunawaan. Higit pa rito, hindi maaaring magpalagay ang bosonic circuit representation tungkol sa truncation at boson-to-qubit encoding na ilalapat sa susunod. Pareho silang pumapasok lamang sa oras ng transpile.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deprecation policy {#deprecation-policy}"
msgstr "Patakaran sa deprecation {#deprecation-policy}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We follow [semantic versioning](https://semver.org/) and are guided by the principles in [Qiskit’s deprecation policy](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/blob/main/DEPRECATION.md). We may occasionally make breaking changes in order to improve the user experience. When possible, we will keep old interfaces and mark them as deprecated, as long as they can co-exist with the new ones. Each substantial improvement, breaking change, or deprecation will be documented in the [release notes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/release-notes).\n"
msgstr "Sinusunod namin ang [semantic versioning](https://semver.org/) at ginagabayan kami ng mga prinsipyo sa [patakaran sa deprecation ng Qiskit](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/blob/main/DEPRECATION.md). Paminsan-minsan ay maaari kaming gumawa ng mga breaking change para mapabuti ang karanasan ng user. Kung maaari, pananatilihin namin ang mga lumang interface at mamarkahan ang mga ito bilang deprecated, hangga't maaari silang mag-co-exist sa mga bago. Idodokumento sa [release notes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/release-notes) ang bawat malaking pagpapabuti, breaking change, o deprecation.\n"

